  "question": "A very special island is inhabited only by sages and fools. Sages always tell the truth, and fools always lie. You meet 5 inhabitants: Mia, Emily, Sophia, Sebastian, and Penelope. \"it is not the case that (Mia is a sage if and only if Emily is a fool)\" - Mia. Emily commented, \"Emily is a sage if and only if (Sebastian is a fool)\". \"(Emily is a fool and Sebastian is a sage) and (Mia is a fool if and only if Sophia is a sage),\" Sophia claimed. As Sebastian put it, \"if (Mia is a fool or Sophia is a fool or Penelope is a fool) then (Penelope is a fool if and only if Sophia is a sage)\". Penelope said, \"(Sophia is a sage) or (Sophia is a fool and Penelope is a sage and Mia is a sage) or (Mia is a sage).\" So who is a sage and who is a fool? (Format your answer like: \"Mia is a sage/fool, Emily is a sage/fool, Sophia is a sage/fool, Sebastian is a sage/fool, and Penelope is a sage/fool\")\n\nIMPORTANT: When you finish, put ONLY the final answer inside \\boxed{...} (no extra text). If the task requests a multi-line format, encode it into a single line representation.",
